<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
     Device overlay for the Meizu M2 Note (m2note, M571) — LineageOS 20.0.

     Carried from the overlay of the LOS 15.1 tree that was built for this
     handset (/srv/forge/android/meizu_m6/rom-lineage-15.1-meizu_m6-experimental/
     device/meizu/m2note/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml).

     Every name below was checked against
     frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/*.xml in THIS tree on 2026-09-16.  An
     unknown name in an overlay is an aapt2 error, not a no-op, so the
     following entries from the 15.1 overlay were DROPPED because the resource
     no longer exists in Android 13:

       config_wifi_background_scan_support   (gone — verified MISSING)
       config_wifi_dual_band_support         (gone — verified MISSING)
       config_dozeAfterScreenOff             (gone — verified MISSING)

     Dropped on purpose although the names still resolve:

       networkAttributes / radioAttributes — the 15.1 arrays describe the
         Nougat/Oreo connectivity model.  Carrying a stale set wholesale is how
         subtle data-connection bugs get inherited; they go back in when
         someone checks them against A13's ConnectivityService, not before.
       config_multiuserMaximumUsers / config_enableMultiUserUI — multi-user on
         a 1792 MiB /system with 3 GB RAM is a space and memory decision, not a
         device-capability one.  Left at AOSP defaults.
       config_persistentDataPackageName=com.google.android.gms — this is a
         LineageOS build with no GMS.  Pointing the FRP package at a package
         that is not installed is worse than leaving it unset.

     Kept despite being unverified on this handset, with the reason:
       config_supportDoubleTapWake=true — asserted by the 15.1 tree, never
         measured on this unit.  HYPOTHESIS; disproved the moment a double tap
         on a sleeping screen does nothing.
-->
<resources xmlns:xliff="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2">

